ADDENDA <Act No. 15214, Dec. 12, 2017>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 3 months after the date of its promulgation; provided, Articles 2, 3, and 5 of the Addenda shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Preparatory committee for the establishment of the National Assembly Futures Institute)
(1) The Speaker shall organize and operate a preparatory committee for the establishment of the National Assembly Futures Institute (hereinafter referred to as the "preparatory committee for establishment") within 1 month from the date of promulgation of this Act to handle affairs relating to the establishment of the NAFI.
(2) The preparatory committee for establishment shall be comprised of not more than 5 members appointed or commissioned by the Speaker in consultation with the floor leaders of each negotiating group.
(3) The preparatory committee for establishment shall prepare the articles of incorporation of the NAFI and obtain permission from the Speaker.
(4) Upon obtaining permission under paragraph (3), the preparatory committee for establishment shall, without delay, register the establishment of the NAFI under joint signature and transfer administrative affairs to the president.
(5) The preparatory committee for establishment shall be deemed dissolved upon completion of the transfer of duties under paragraph (4), and the members of the preparatory committee for establishment shall be deemed dismissed or removed from office.
Article 3 (Establishment expenses)
Expenses incurred for the establishment of the NAFI until its establishment shall be borne by the Secretariat of the National Assembly.
Article 4 (Succession of Rights and obligations)
(1) The NAFI established under this Act shall comprehensively succeed to the rights and obligations of the preparatory committee for establishment.
(2) The name of the preparatory committee for establishment stated in the register of the rights and obligations to which the NAFI comprehensively succeeds under paragraph (1), or in other public records, shall be deemed the name of the NAFI.
(3) Any act performed by or toward the preparatory committee for establishment shall be deemed an act performed by or toward the NAFI.
Article 5 (Special cases concerning request for budget)
Notwithstanding Article 19, the preparatory committee for establishment may prepare the budget request and business plan of the NAFI for the first business year commencing after its establishment.
Article 6 (Special cases concerning term of office of executive officers)
Notwithstanding Article 8, the term of office of executive officers appointed or commissioned for the first time after this Act enters into force shall expire upon the expiration of the term of office of the members of the 20th National Assembly.
